WEBVTT

00:00:06.812 --> 00:00:07.412
The name's Brogan.

00:00:07.964 --> 00:00:08.684
Lieutenant Brogan.

00:00:10.396 --> 00:00:13.396
For 20 years, I was with the NYPD. Now?

00:00:13.884 --> 00:00:16.444
Well, let's just say I've transferred to another precinct.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:30.320
See ya.

00:01:36.844 --> 00:01:37.344
temple.

00:01:37.804 --> 00:01:39.104
It's exquisite, sister man.

00:01:39.852 --> 00:01:40.892
Thank you, my Anka.

00:01:41.356 --> 00:01:43.836
I was guided by your spirit in its design.

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:45.456
Not mine, I'm afraid.

00:01:45.896 --> 00:01:48.096
I could not create a flaw, let alone...

00:01:48.364 --> 00:01:49.364
an entire temple.

00:01:50.092 --> 00:01:51.232
Is it not impressive?

00:01:52.268 --> 00:01:53.328
It is impressive.

00:01:54.028 --> 00:01:55.688
But I'm not at all surprised.

00:01:56.012 --> 00:01:58.892
Sister Nevek has always been full of designs.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.960
Fellow pirates, behold the eternal flame, symbol of...

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.020
Our faith from its humble origin centuries ago to its new beginning of this day.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:12.950
We hereby consecrate this temple to the spirit of fireism, the purity of fire, flame without end.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.670
Let it be so.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:15.640
Thank you.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:07.320
There is a traitor in our midst, a heretic who pretends to share our sacred views,

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.840
but who is motivated by power and greed.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:24.420
He is false to the fire. He has no fire in his heart, but there shall be.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.500
This is me riding a curcuin.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.720
P.S. We ate it for dinner.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.970
Aw, weeks of no way and the guys finally lost it.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:54.880
I don't think Hal Day never had it.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:58.860
One thing, he's gonna kick himself for missing this one.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:04:59.980
Oh, I don't...

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.960
Spontaneous combustion, see it all the time.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:13.100
Never seen anything like it.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.900
There was no physical contact, nothing out of the ordinary.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.970
Tookie, a woman pointed a finger and a man burst into flames.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.270
I'd say that was out of the ordinary.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.720
She's a priest, Lieutenant.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.140
Sister Nevik Brock, the Icar Vedra's right hand.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.140
Uh, what's an Icar Vedra?

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.440
The Ikar is the Pyrus spiritual leader.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.570
He's an extraordinary man.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.480
You a Pyrus, Tookie?

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:43.100
I guess I'm looking for the answers without knowing all the questions.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.960
Sounds like what we do for a living.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:52.270
Tendhal Galiki was a good man, but nothing.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.930
You need to relax. The Herbs will help.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:57.530
I loved him like a son.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.580
And he thought you were a fool.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:05:59.980
Brother...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.090
Calamandro forgive me my Icar I cannot remain silent any longer to your face

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:12.340
he was one way behind your back another is this so it's your own goodness which

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:16.680
blinds you to the evil of others and you said nothing you know the words of the

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:25.900
Daskal there is justice in the fire I'm sorry to disturb you my Icar but the

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:29.940
police they wish to interview you you rest I'll take

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:39.010
care of this see you back at the station house all right lieutenant brogan this is a sister nevic

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:47.350
brock she's the one who uh well you what the officer is trying to say is somehow i became the

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:54.370
medium for divine intervention i see um you don't think it could be a little more specific you may

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:59.980
find it difficult to believe but a miracle occurred here earlier tendal kaliki was pure

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.260
by the eternal flame in his heart he betrayed us and his heart betrayed him

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:12.710
lieutenant I refuse to believe that brother Tendall was a heretic I've known

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:19.760
him since I came here as a seeker he was a good kind man is it possible that

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:24.640
anybody here considered him a threat yes tell us sister Fancher maybe you're

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:28.420
aware of something I am not no sister Nevick

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.370
Now that you've seen our temple's soul, perhaps you'd like to see the brain.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:36.060
We oversee many technical details there.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.560
Tell you what, why don't you take officers Oren and Castle?

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.020
Yes, of course. Follow me.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:54.910
Anything?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:56.200
Vilch.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.860
in the passageway behind the wall.

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:35.140
Go stand in the spot where the priest was killed.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:36.910
No problem, Lieutenant.

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:43.530
All right, I'm here.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.130
Yeah, so I see.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:51.000
This all looks pretty sophisticated.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:52.540
Not really.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:55.040
Just normal security screens,

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:58.630
processes to control the temple's exterior illumination,

00:08:58.750 --> 00:08:59.450
that sort of thing.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:08:59.980
We are.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:15.130
very lucky to have brother cam and his special expertise can i help you officer brother calamandro

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:21.940
yeah what's all this these tanks contain fuel for the flames outside the temple

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:28.490
or did you think that was a miracle also i don't believe in miracles pity

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:36.060
At this point, given the condition of the remains, the coroner can only determine that Kaliki burned to death.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.060
Ah, well, now, that's a revelation, isn't it?

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:41.020
And he was pretty sure that the fire began in Kaliki's heart.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:43.770
Has he enlightened us as to how that could have happened?

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:44.470
Afraid not.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:45.810
Have you any ideas?

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:48.370
Could be microwaves, possibly delta waves.

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:52.350
Neither would be detectable in an autopsy, but that's only speculation, of course.

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.010
There's at least one other possibility, Captain.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:55.800
Chook.

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.970
The Daskal, the Pyrus Bible, tells the story of a disciple...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.000
whose heart burst into flames because his thoughts were impure.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.060
I'm not quite sure how to respond to that.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:10.240
Uh, Carson, I noticed a small diameter hole in one of the altar room walls.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.700
It looks like it was lined up with the spot where Kaliki was standing.

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.970
Well, microwaves would only need a pen point to do the job.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.640
Has anyone found a microwave-generating device?

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:21.780
We searched the place from top to bottom. Nothing.

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:24.680
Then we have no hard evidence, do we, Lieutenant?

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:26.240
No, sir.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.940
Look, people, we're treading a fine line here.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.300
These pirates are protected by the laws governing freedom of religious practice.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:36.460
If they cry foul, I don't need to tell you how difficult our job will become.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:39.810
Took, you're a member of this cult, correct?

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.470
Not really, sir.

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:45.170
It was only my second visit, and it's not exactly a cult.

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:47.950
Whatever it is, I want you to keep your eyes open whenever you're there.

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:51.000
Remember, you're a police officer, 26 hours a day.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:51.980
Yes, sir.

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:53.300
There's one other thing, Captain.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.300
Kaliki's feet have been burned before.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:57.350
They were scarred over and calloused.

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:58.980
Coroner doesn't know what to make of it.

00:10:59.330 --> 00:10:59.970
Well, it's not...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.200
Ah, let's invite the Bruck woman in for our chat.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:04.870
Perhaps she can enlighten us.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.850
And this one couldn't tell you what you needed to know?

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:11.660
I only recently became a seeker, Sister Nevick.

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:12.270
Ah.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.790
Seekers are not official members of our order.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.920
If they choose to join us, then they become initiates.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:21.000
After much work and study, an initiate becomes an acolyte.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:22.910
Like Brother Calamandro?

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:26.440
Yes. A very few of us, like Brother Tendal and myself,

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:28.100
are called to become priests.

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:29.960
Hmm. Maybe...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.380
It's just me, but what's all that's got to do with Tenokaliki's feet?

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:38.920
Every priest must undertake periodic firewalks over molten lava

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.680
to prove the strength of our belief.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:46.740
As a result, all priests have scarred and blackened feet.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:53.400
That's proper.

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.520
Sister Nevik is my correct title.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.980
Sister Nevik, thank you for coming in to talk to us.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.060
You really think that I killed Brother Tendall, don't you?

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.310
Pyrism is a benevolent belief, Sergeant.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.160
We have no wish to harm anyone, not even a traitor.

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:12.880
Well, Lieutenant is my correct title, sister,

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.380
and somebody sure as hell harmed Tendall Kaliki.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:19.080
Is it so impossible for you to believe that he might have done it to himself,

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:24.130
that a heart in conflict with itself might just explode in flames?

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:26.590
Yeah, it is.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.570
And how did you know his heart was the source of the fire?

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:31.920
The Daskal says it was so.

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.640
You want to try reading it sometime, Lieutenant?

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.080
Then you too might find the fire.

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:53.980
You're not actually going to go through with a fire ceremony for Kaliki.

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:57.910
Now that the authorities have returned his remains, yes.

00:12:58.480 --> 00:12:59.980
But what were the congregations...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.640
Perhaps they will say that it is the proper thing to do.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.340
Or that you are going against the Daskal.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.420
What will you say?

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.370
It doesn't matter what I say, I'm only one.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:18.540
But it is difficult to explain why you feel compelled to honor a heretic.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.840
Because my heart is unconvinced.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.980
To me, Lindel Kaliki will always be innocent.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.640
You heard what Calamandro said.

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:29.970
Kaliki spoke...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:35.140
against you. If he had things to say against me, he would have said them to me.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:40.440
Father Tyndall will be granted a full-fire ceremony. He lived as a loyal

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:45.730
Pyreist. He would be remembered as one. I warn you, my Icar, if you go through with

00:13:45.730 --> 00:13:52.520
this, it could divide the church. So, sister, what are my choices? If I do as

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:58.580
my conscience dictates, yes, I could divide the church. But if I ignore my

00:13:58.580 --> 00:13:58.980
conscience.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.380
I will be a leader in name only.

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:05.950
Better, I think, a feeble-minded Icar Vhaedra

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.420
than a cowardly one.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.860
You worry too much.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.180
Because my Icar, you worry too little.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:09.420
I am guilty. I have sinned.

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:10.680
Brother Tyndall.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:17.000
I sought not piety, but gold and glory.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:21.920
I am unworthy. May the fire forgive me.

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.430
You old man.

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:32.370
Maybe now you'll believe her.

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:45.790
Questioning what you saw, Took, I just want to know how it was done.

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:51.160
Well, I have questioned it, Captain, and I'm pretty sure I found the answer in the Daskal.

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:55.710
You know, Took, we've programmed slow-mo to reconstruct voices.

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:57.900
Maybe the pirates did something similar.

00:15:58.260 --> 00:15:59.960
Don't patronize me, Lieutenant. I know...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.080
what I saw. Look, I know you're skeptical, but sometimes you gotta believe in something bigger,

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:11.760
something greater. Tookie, I'm just a carver, not a theologian, but I'm a tough old nut to crack.

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:20.000
It's my nature. So, uh, humor me and, uh, keep looking around, huh? Yes, sir. May I go now?

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:29.970
Yeah. You take her off the investigation? Nah, she'll be okay.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.680
She just wants us to keep an open mind.

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.960
What about you? Are you a believer?

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:38.980
Certainly not in pirism.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:40.020
In anything?

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:44.300
Well, if Haldane didn't get back from vacation pretty soon,

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:48.400
I believe that I'm gonna drown in all the paperwork that's piling up on her desk.

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:54.540
Why are we questioning the authority of the Icarvedra?

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.360
The poor man is senile.

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:58.680
How dare you?

00:16:58.800 --> 00:16:59.980
Because someone might...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:06.090
the Icar is old so old he cannot even recognize the omens that were foretold

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:12.930
were they omens brother Calamandro or something else a false prophet set aflame

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:18.950
by his own evil a corpse who confesses his sins from the other side a child

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:23.790
could recognize such signs and I say that the Icar Vedra is our appointed

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:29.790
leader it is he and he alone who has the power to recognize the omens sister

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:29.970
next

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.660
Kravik, what do you say?

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:34.810
I don't know. I admit I'm torn.

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:37.410
I love and respect the Icar Vedra,

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:39.370
but even I can't ignore the signs.

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:42.200
Perhaps the day of immolation is near.

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:44.990
We've all seen the signs.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.390
Only the Icar is blind.

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:49.750
And who would you have replaced him?

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:51.690
You, brother?

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:56.950
Me. I will never be loved enough to lead.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.480
But there is one among us who could.

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.580
One through whom the fire has spoken?

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:03.410
No.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:05.470
Brother Calamandra, thank you.

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:08.110
But my loyalty is to the Ikar Vedra.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:11.850
Your loyalty, Sister Nevik, shouldn't be to a man.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:14.260
It should be to the fire.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:25.870
This stuff is creepy.

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:28.520
It's all fire this and fire that.

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:29.960
May you find the...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:37.230
fire may the fire be with you it's stupid yeah they believe the end of the world is coming they

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:45.280
call it the day of imitation immolation brainless matt anyway the guys at school think it's dumb

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:55.730
they just goof on it yeah why i told you it's dumb it's silly let it be so come on dad get

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:59.880
virtual you don't believe this stuff no but there might be

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.700
I do believe that the pirates think are silly and dumb.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:04.160
That doesn't mean I want them laughing at me.

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:05.520
Why don't you just say that, Daddy?

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:06.240
Am I?

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:07.900
So you agree with them?

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:11.970
I think what your father is saying is that beliefs are a very personal thing,

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:15.310
maybe even a sacred thing, whether you agree with them or not.

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:18.210
As long as they're not harming anyone, you respect other people's belief,

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:19.350
even if you think they're dumb,

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:22.220
the same way you want them to respect your beliefs.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:23.740
I get it.

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:29.410
So it means if I believe I should go downtown to that reality arcade with the Nazi,

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:29.970
You'd receive.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:35.220
Yeah, we'd respect it, but actually letting you do it, I believe not.

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:37.890
Next try, man.

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:39.470
It was so close.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:42.410
Have some relish.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:43.370
Have some tongs.

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:46.220
Relish?

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:51.000
No, what's up?

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:53.440
Got a call on hold from a sister, Fancher.

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:55.040
She's down at the Pyrus Temple.

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:57.320
She asked for you, said it was urgent.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:58.300
Patch her through.

00:19:59.620 --> 00:19:59.980
Sister F...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:07.310
Fancher. Lieutenant, I need to talk to you. I'm listening. No, not here. It's not safe.

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:12.340
Is there somewhere, not the station house, someplace we can meet privately?

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:37.560
She took the hopper.

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:38.920
Yeah, good.

00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:35.820
Purify her.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:12.260
You're damn right I'm taking it personally.

00:22:12.380 --> 00:22:14.580
They killed Fancher and they almost nailed me in the bargain.

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:16.440
She could have been on a suicide mission.

00:22:16.990 --> 00:22:17.630
You didn't talk to her.

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:19.010
Well, maybe it was an accident.

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:20.050
Soap could be right.

00:22:20.210 --> 00:22:22.570
We found nothing in the records that indicates sabotage.

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:23.750
Yeah, right, an accident.

00:22:23.910 --> 00:22:25.970
Just like Tyndall Collini's death was a miracle.

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:28.940
Bottom line here, people, we've got no facts.

00:22:29.180 --> 00:22:29.780
Just coincidence.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.280
Like my grandpa used to say, if there wasn't such a thing...

00:22:33.280 --> 00:22:34.640
We wouldn't need a word for you.

00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:37.460
Well, I don't believe in coincidences, and I don't believe in miracles.

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:41.540
I'm telling you, Fancher knew something, and when she tried to tell me, they eliminated it.

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:43.900
Ah, speculation, coincidences, call it what you will.

